        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T16:28:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not `kOutOfMemory`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 799,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 799,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "46501b5d3261344792e134fa2f87d83493f56400",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae19fc15_229021fe",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 799,
      "author": {
        "id": 4772438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T17:20:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is to match libpng: my understanding is that `kOutOfMemory` is specifically for when you go over memory budget (as declared by the caller), whereas `kInternalError` is used for allocation failures (e.g. you could be within budget, yet fail to allocate due to environment memory constraints).",
      "parentUuid": "5b881d0b_b8f0989e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 799,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 799,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "46501b5d3261344792e134fa2f87d83493f56400",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ce8566b_b232e114",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 799,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T21:31:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Huh.  Thanks for explaining.  SGTM.",
      "parentUuid": "ae19fc15_229021fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 799,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 799,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "46501b5d3261344792e134fa2f87d83493f56400",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07620d76_3e55fa26",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T16:28:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems a bit unfortunate that `fPreblendBuffer` and `fPreblendBufferStorage` are separate fields - the former may become dangling.  I think that ideally \"somebody\" (common/shared/base part of Skia?) would provide a `BudgetedVector` as a single abstraction.\n\nOTOH I understand that this is beyond the scope of this CL.  /cc @fmalita",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "46501b5d3261344792e134fa2f87d83493f56400",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84f0a6f3_2fb0d63f",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 4772438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T17:20:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See other comment: note that `sk_calloc_canfail` isn’t related to the budget here, but rather allocation failures (the budget is checked and updated before the actual allocation), so I’m not sure if \"budget\" would be the right term",
      "parentUuid": "07620d76_3e55fa26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "46501b5d3261344792e134fa2f87d83493f56400",
